This project demonstrates:

Java + Spring Boot backend development.

RESTful API design.

Database integration using JPA/Hibernate.

CRUD operations with tasks.


Technologies Used########################

Java 21

Spring Boot (with JPA & Hibernate)

Maven (for build management)

MySQL (relational database)

##############################################################
User sends HTTP requests to the API.

Spring Boot controllers handle the request and delegate to the service layer.

Service layer interacts with the database using JPA repositories.

The response is sent back in JSON format.

#########################################################
Prerequisites

Java 21 installed

Maven installed (mvn -v)

MySQL running

List of APIs of the project 
*********************************************
GET	/api/tasks	Get all tasks
GET	/api/tasks/{id}	Get a single task by ID
POST	/api/tasks	Create a new task
PUT	/api/tasks/{id}	Update an existing task
DELETE	/api/tasks/{id}	Delete a task
POST http://localhost:8080/api/tasks/process-sync
POST http://localhost:8080/api/tasks/{id}/queue-delete
POST http://localhost:8080/api/tasks/{id}/queue-sync
******************************************************
